{"title":"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain land, all Arogs are Brafs, all Crups are Brafs, all Dramps are Arogs, and all Crups are Dramps. Which of the following statements is implied by these facts?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fadfb20bf2479e27579c5163975ea22b86bde885.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } \\text{All Dramps are Brafs and are Crups.}\\\\ \\textbf{(B) } \\text{All Brafs are Crups and are Dramps.}\\\\ \\textbf{(C) } \\text{All Arogs are Crups and are Dramps.}\\\\ \\textbf{(D) } \\text{All Crups are Arogs and are Brafs.}\\\\ \\textbf{(E) } \\text{All Arogs are Dramps and some Arogs may not be Crups.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"455\" height=\"96\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/7/4f789d67c624d86c7eaf0debff6651106b4c62a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] unitsize(6mm); defaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(9pt)); dotfactor=4;  real r1=1, r2=2, r3=3, r4=4; pair O1=(0,0), O2=(0,-0.5), O3=(0,-1), O4=(0,-1.5); path circleA=Circle(O1,r1); draw(circleA); path circleB=Circle(O2,r2); draw(circleB); path circleC=Circle(O3,r3); draw(circleC); path circleD=Circle(O4,r4); draw(circleD);  label(&quot;$Crups$&quot;,(0,-.5)); label(&quot;$Dramps$&quot;,(0,-2)); label(&quot;$Arogs$&quot;,(0,-3.5)); label(&quot;$Brafs$&quot;,(0,-5)); [/asy]\" width=\"228\" height=\"228\" /></center>\n<p>It may be easier to visualize this by drawing some sort of diagram. From the first statement, you can draw an Arog circle inside of the Braf circle, since all Arogs are Brafs, but not all Brafs are Arogs. Ignore the second statement for now, and draw a Dramp circle in the Arog circle and a Crup circle in the Dramp circle. You can see the second statement is already true because all Crups are Arogs. As you can see, the only statement that is true is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/3/d53b37edf32cfbc0179e6e6cd9b2ff4d482b6634.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(D)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"29\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's replace the terms with some more familiar terms. Let \"Arogs\" be math problems, \"Brafs\" be problems, \"Crups\" be 2007 AMC 10 problems, and \"Dramps\" be AMC 10 problems. All the statements then hold. Let us now analyze the claims individually.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/6/a46f6af01fcf3bb5f6cac2316bc4de9bb3906bec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> All AMC 10 problems are problems and 2007 AMC 10 problems. This statement is false.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> All problems are 2007 AMC 10 problems and AMC 10 problems. This statement is false.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/9/169b8d69bd74a91e72ec43123070d770633a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> All math problems are 2007 AMC 10 problems and AMC 10 problems. This statement is false.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> All 2007 AMC 10 problems are math problems and problems. This statement is true.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e41e3cd48cee2c6866cfbb4386a8e99d3482f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> All math problems are AMC 10 problems and some math problems may not be 2007 AMC 10 problems. This statement is false.\n</p><p>Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/3/1c31941c2b9f0b023af387b303864c1351871e3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}~\\text{All Crups are Arogs and are Brafs.}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"303\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ cxsmi\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B\">2007 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2007 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" cl